                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.5431/256: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bern</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-10-26T11:00:00+01:00">October 26, 1935—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 26—6:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>43. Department’s 66, October 23, 2 p.m. Culbertson and Hawks saw Stucki last
                    evening. He stated that Swiss watch manufacturers recently told him that if the
                    present American proposals on watches are not bettered they would prefer that no
                    agreement be signed since tariff on adjusted movements makes their position
                    worse instead of better. Stucki telegraphed Nef on the 23rd to investigate and
                    report. I am seeing Stucki Monday and would appreciate Department’s comment on
                    the above prior to that time.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
